{"id":"torrey:husbands","source":"torrey","name":"Husbands","slug":"husbands","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Should have but one wife — Ge 2:24; Mr 10:6-8; 1Co 7:2-4.","refs":[["Gen",2,24,2,24],["Mark",10,6,10,8],["1Cor",7,2,7,4]]},{"text":"Have authority over their wives — Ge 3:16; 1Co 11:3; Eph 5:23.","refs":[["Gen",3,16,3,16],["1Cor",11,3,11,3],["Eph",5,23,5,23]]},{"text":"To respect them. — 1Pe 3:7.","refs":[["1Pet",3,7,3,7]]},{"text":"To love them. — Eph 5:25-33; Col 3:19.","refs":[["Eph",5,25,5,33],["Col",3,19,3,19]]},{"text":"To regard them as themselves. — Ge 2:23; Mt 19:5.","refs":[["Gen",2,23,2,23],["Matt",19,5,19,5]]},{"text":"To be faithful to them. — Pr 5:19; Mal 2:14,15.","refs":[["Prov",5,19,5,19],["Mal",2,14,2,14],["Mal",2,15,2,15]]},{"text":"To dwell with them for life. — Ge 2:24; Mt 19:3-9.","refs":[["Gen",2,24,2,24],["Matt",19,3,19,9]]},{"text":"To comfort them. — 1Sa 1:8.","refs":[["1Sam",1,8,1,8]]},{"text":"To consult with them. — Ge 31:4-7.","refs":[["Gen",31,4,31,7]]},{"text":"Not to leave them, though unbelieving. — 1Co 7:11,12,14,16.","refs":[["1Cor",7,11,7,11],["1Cor",7,12,7,12],["1Cor",7,14,7,14],["1Cor",7,16,7,16]]},{"text":"Duties of, not to interfere with their duties to Christ — Lu 14:26; Mt 19:29.","refs":[["Luke",14,26,14,26],["Matt",19,29,19,29]]},{"text":"Isaac. — Ge 24:67.","refs":[["Gen",24,67,24,67]]},{"text":"Elkanah. — 1Sa 1:4,5.","refs":[["1Sam",1,4,1,4],["1Sam",1,5,1,5]]},{"text":"Solomon. — 1Ki 11:1.","refs":[["1Kgs",11,1,11,1]]},{"text":"Ahasuerus. — Es 1:10,11.","refs":[["Esth",1,10,1,10],["Esth",1,11,1,11]]}],"refCount":30}
